Admin merge has exactly ONE sanctioned use: bypassing the missing-secondary-reviewer / self-review requirement. To use it, record that plainly:

  "merge": { "admin": true, "admin_reason": "missing-secondary-reviewer" }

That is the only accepted value. It may never stand in for a red check or a merge conflict — both are already denied above.

gates.message:
Closing an issue is terminal and outward, so it needs a recorded basis: a diagnosis (defect lane — not-a-bug / already-fixed) or a decision record (enhancement / feature lane).

Shape: {"decisions":[{"issue":123,"lane":"enhancement","verdict":"deny","source":"AskUserQuestion","rationale":"..."}]}

`source` is the load-bearing field: this lane exists to give the maintainer a decision, not to make it for them. If you did not ask, there is no verdict to record and no close to perform.
